    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="7">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Ine">Ine</ref> 7</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="7" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="92" ed="#liebermann"/>LI. Gif hwa stalie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#Ine_7.lnote.oe.15-2"/>, swa his wíf nyte ⁊ his bearn, geselle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Ine_7.lnote.oe.13-2"/> LX<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#Ine_7.lnote.oe.16-2"/> scill. to wite.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="7" corresp="#wit-bu"><pb n="92" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif hwa sta . . ., . . selle LX scill. . . . . .</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="7" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="92" ed="#liebermann"/>LI. Gif hwa stalige, swa his wif (hit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Ine_7.lnote.oe.9"/>) nyte ⁊ his bearn, gesylle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_7.lnote.oe.3"/> LX scll' to wite.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="7" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="93" ed="#liebermann"/>Be stale. Gyf hwá stalige, swa his wif nyte ⁊ his bearn, gesylle syxti scill' to wite.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="7" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="93" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis furetur sic, ut uxor eius<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Ine_7.lnote.oe.13"/> nesciat (hoc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#Ine_7.lnote.oe.14"/>) et<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#Ine_7.lnote.oe.15"/> pueri sui, reddat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#Ine_7.lnote.oe.16"/> wite LX sol.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="38" ed="#attenborough"/>[Be stale.] Gif hwa stalie, swa his wíf<ptr type="editorNote" n="12" target="#Ine_7.attnote.fn.12"/> nyte ⁊ his bearn, geselle LX scill. to wite.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="7" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="376" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>{LI} Gif swa stalie, swa his wíf nyte ⁊ his bearn, geselle LX sciƚƚ to wite.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="93" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn einer stiehlt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_7.lnote.de.1"/>, vorausgesetzt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_7.lnote.de.2"/>, sein Weib<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_7.lnote.de.3"/> und seine Nachkommenschaft wissen [es] nicht, so gebe er 60 Schill.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_7.lnote.de.4"/> zur Strafe.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If someone steals, provided his wife and his offspring do not know [of it], let him give 60 shillings as a fine.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="39" ed="#attenborough"/>If anyone steals<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Ine_7.attnote.n.1"/> without the cognisance of his wife and children, he shall pay a fine of 60 shillings.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="400" ed="#whitelock"/>If anyone steals without his wife and his children knowing, he is to pay 60 shillings as a fine.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="377" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If someone steals, but his wife and his child(ren) do not know it, let him pay 60 shillings as a fine.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="377"><label>another instance</label> <ref target="clause:Wi_12-a">Wi 12</ref> <quote>For another instance of the separate culpability of husband and wife see Wihtred §9 [L12].</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="278"><label>contradicts</label> <ref target="clause:Af_9-2">Af 9.2</ref> <quote>where Ine called sixty shillings the 'full fine' with evident reference to theft, Alfred stipulated that 120 shillings was to be the fine for all thefts (n. 72)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-ppmel" n="127"><label>difficult to reconcile with</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_7-1">Ine 7.1</ref> <quote>Ine 7:1 ... decreeing slavery for a whole household ... is difficult to reconcile with the 60 shilling fine for thieves acting alone in Ine 7 (cf. ... Ine 53</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="421"><label>compare</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_57">Ine 57</ref> <quote>For a somewhat different interpretation of the wife's liability, compare §7.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="305"><label>?Alfredian penalty; contrast Ine</label> <ref target="clause:IIAs_1">II As 1–1.5</ref> <quote>enforce the (?Alfredian) penalty of 120 shillings on those convicted by due process; Ine had merely forbidden vendetta for thieves killed in flagrante, and his penalty for others seems to have been 60 shillings</quote></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_7.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">93</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_7.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">93</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_7.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">93</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">neque <hi rend="italic">MHkBr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">neque MHkBr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_7.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">93</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-ant <hi rend="italic">T</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-ant T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_7.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">92</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">übergeschr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">written above</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_7.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">92</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">y <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">y on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_7.lnote.oe.15-2" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">92</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">stalige <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">stalige Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_7.lnote.oe.13-2" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">92</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">gesylle <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">gesylle Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_7.lnote.oe.16-2" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">92</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">syxtig <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">syxtig Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_7.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">69</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Diebstahl 19</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Diebstahl 19</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_7.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">69</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Wb: swa</hi> III D [‘so dass’ Toller V 5] = <hi rend="italic">gif heo facnes gewita nære</hi> VI As 1, 1</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Wb: swa</hi> III D [‘so that’ Toller V 5] = <hi rend="italic">gif heo facnes gewita nære</hi> VI As 1, 1</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_7.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">69</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Ehefrau 9—10d</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Ehefrau 9—10d</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_7.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">69</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Die Tat ist nicht handhaft</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The offence is not one caught in the act</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_7.attnote.fn.12" n="12" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">38</biblScope></bibl><label>wíf</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">wif</hi> (<hi rend="italic">hit</hi>). H*.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Ine_7.attnote.n.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">184</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">There is an apparent contradiction between this law and Ine, cap. 12. Liebermann understands that in the latter case, in contradistinction to this, the reference is to a thief caught in the act (cf. Wiht. cap. 26; II As. cap. 1).</seg></note>
      </div>
